Subject: [PATCH] exclude qwen4exp from LLAMA_SPLIT_MODE_TENSOR

--split-mode tensor silently corrupts Qwen3.8-Flash-Next output: fluent
nonsense, no error, and ~45%% faster than the correct path. Its ssm_* tensors
collide by name with the Mamba-style split patterns without sharing their
semantics, and its fused multi-input ops cannot be made split-consistent
without mirroring most of the block.

With this patch that configuration fails at load with a clear message; the
single-node path is unaffected.

See benchmarks/qwen4exp-tensor-split-corruption.md
---
--- a/src/llama-arch.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-arch.cpp
@@ -1145,6 +1145,12 @@
         case LLM_ARCH_MINIMAX_M3:
         case LLM_ARCH_MISTRAL4:
         case LLM_ARCH_KIMI_LINEAR:
+        // qwen4exp: hybrid attention/SSM. Its ssm_* tensors collide by name with
+        // the Mamba-style split patterns without sharing their semantics, and its
+        // fused multi-input ops cannot be made split-consistent without mirroring
+        // most of the block. Tensor split here produces SILENTLY WRONG OUTPUT
+        // (fluent nonsense, no error) while running faster than the correct path.
+        case LLM_ARCH_QWEN4EXP:
         case LLM_ARCH_BAILINGMOE3:
         case LLM_ARCH_KIMI_K3:
         case LLM_ARCH_QWEN3TTS:
